  "sentence": "The stall reproduces under the library default initialisation (3/3 seeds, mean last-ten loss 0.9866) and disappears under dit_zero (0/3 seeds stall, mean last-ten loss 0.4164), so on this toy the stall is initialisation-dependent. dit_zero is the arm that actually carries exactly-zero AdaLN gates and final projections, and it is the arm that escapes; library_default (Diffusers ada_norm_zero default, gates NOT zero) and dit_standard (Xavier, gates not zero) both stall. The specific 'zero-initialised residual gates caused the stall' attribution is therefore contradicted even though initialisation-dependence holds; the rewrite must say so.",
